#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:5
#: 8bbb67cd10d04b86bafa88ec7ac7d5bb
msgid "Choosing Your Rover Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:7
#: c325a0751025461e8120aee153a07e39
msgid "Setting up your Rover requires a collection of various hardware components. This guide is designed to help you understand these essential pieces of equipment, offering both necessary requirements and additional recommendations for optimal performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:10
#: c6a128479d224f45bd9d7592cb01ce28
msgid "RC Transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:12
#: 05eced84b74547e8830e35e832d889d8
msgid "The RC (Radio Control) transmitter allows you to manually control your Rover and toggle through its various control modes. You can use any RC transmitter/receiver system, provided it has a minimum of four channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:17
#: 8333668d5d0545d589df0574894059fb
msgid "While choosing an RC Transmitter, consider the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:19
#: a0405013c0cf46e4982756d7a004789b
msgid "Avoid transmitters designed specifically for cars as they come with a steering wheel and throttle trigger which are not conducive for controlling a Rover with different driving modes and additional features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:20
#: b9e32503e5044469a9128715db4555a6
msgid "A transmitter with at least two toggle switches is preferred, with one of these having three distinct positions for various controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:21
#: 7ce5289d75d547108372fb2c7ae4a3b8
msgid "For budget-conscious users, the `Turnigy 9x <http://hobbyking.com/hobbyking/store/__8992__Turnigy_9X_9Ch_Transmitter_w_Module_8ch_Receiver_Mode_2_v2_Firmware_.html>`__ ($54) is a well-regarded choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:22
#: 5b70c8604e9a42fa818ba255a840bc22
msgid "For those seeking higher quality and more features, consider OpenTX/FrSky systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:24
#: 9cb840e8dc58411ebf82201ef7c5c58d
msgid ":ref:`Compatible RC Transmitter and Receiver Systems <common-rc-systems>` provides a more extensive list of options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:27
#: 650ad30254f340019dcad83609b45251
msgid "GPS Receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:29
#: 1f4892b14c1e4010b7d8a0a80170317f
msgid "A GPS module is an integral part of your Rover setup. The :ref:`UBlox GPS + Compass Module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>` is highly recommended due to its combined GPS and compass functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:31
#: 324c67783b51428a874c87f55b4df130
msgid "For alternative GPS options, refer to :ref:`GPS solutions <common-positioning-landing-page>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:37
#: 97a68b71340f4b2d9c273c7eccb7e8e6
msgid "Batteries and Charger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:39
#: 5edefdd729174102b305143580dab797
msgid "Powering your Rover requires reliable batteries and an efficient charger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:41
#: cf6e5e556dba4503acad2635c967dd72
msgid "For a smaller 1/16 or 1/18 scale Rover, a 2S (7.2v) LiPo battery under 2600 mAh, like `this one <http://hobbyking.com/hobbyking/store/__16589__Turnigy_1700mAh_2S_20C_Lipo_Pack_Suits_1_16th_Monster_Beatle_SCT_Buggy_USA_Warehouse_.html>`__, should suffice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:42
#: 4fdb734a8c4641388f93692542ce81d3
msgid "For larger 1/10th scale Rover, `this is a good size choice <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/zippy-5000mah-2s1p-30c-hardcase-pack.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:43
#: ad6071a098d747429a3530f16d1c114d
msgid "An easy-to-use LiPo charger such as `this one <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/imax-b6-ac-v2-charger-discharger-1-6-cells-genuine-au-plug.html>`__ is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:46
#: e9446b7d581f440fbb4994e195c68935
msgid "Telemetry Radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:48
#: eb5420e292524bdabf9deaae43f5ab33
msgid "The :ref:`telemetry radio <common-telemetry-landingpage>` enables your Rover to communicate with your ground station remotely using the MAVLink protocol. This adds significant capabilities to your Rover, including real-time mission interaction and live data streaming from vehicle-mounted components. Although not compulsory, it is a valuable addition to your Rover setup!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:54
#: c2e5cce89021430f9fbf8431af3d1bb7
msgid "Distance Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/choosing-hardware.rst:56
#: d5cf0a4bd69043e38b14ac50c15a59b4
msgid "If you're looking to equip your Rover with obstacle avoidance capabilities, :ref:`Sonar/IR sensors <sonar-sensors>` are a great choice. These sensors help the Rover detect and avoid objects in its path, enhancing its autonomous navigation abilities."
msgstr ""
